The root cause is that `Microsoft.AspNetCore.OpenApi` 10.0 upgraded from **OpenAPI.NET v1.x to v2.0**, which has several breaking changes. Here's what changed and the fixed code:

### 1. `OpenApiAny` types removed → use `JsonNode`
`OpenApiString`, `OpenApiInteger`, etc. are gone. Use `System.Text.Json.Nodes` instead.

### 2. `Schema.Nullable` removed
OpenAPI 3.1 uses a `type` array with `"null"` instead of a `nullable: true` flag. Check/set via `schema.Type` and `JsonSchemaType.Null`.

### 3. Entities are now interfaces
Types like `OpenApiSchema` may appear as `IOpenApiSchema`. Security scheme references use `OpenApiSecuritySchemeReference`.

### 4. `OpenApiSecurityRequirement` restructured
No longer a `Dictionary<OpenApiSecurityScheme, IList<string>>`.

---

### Fixed code:

```csharp
using System.Text.Json.Nodes;          // replaces Microsoft.OpenApi.Any
using Microsoft.OpenApi.Models;
using Microsoft.OpenApi.Models.Interfaces;
using Microsoft.OpenApi.Models.References;

options.AddOperationTransformer((operation, context, ct) =>
{
    var param = operation.Parameters?.FirstOrDefault(p => p.Name == "api-version");
    if (param is not null)
    {
        // OpenApiString → JsonNode
        param.Schema.Example = JsonValue.Create("1.0");
    }

    // OpenApiResponse unchanged, but Responses may need null-init
    operation.Responses ??= new OpenApiResponses();
    operation.Responses.TryAdd("401",
        new OpenApiResponse { Description = "Unauthorized" });

    // Use OpenApiSecuritySchemeReference instead of
    // OpenApiSecurityScheme + OpenApiReference
    var oAuthRef = new OpenApiSecuritySchemeReference("oauth2");

    operation.Security =
    [
        new OpenApiSecurityRequirement
        {
            Scheme = oAuthRef,
            Scopes = scopes   // List<string>
        }
    ];

    return Task.CompletedTask;
});

options.AddSchemaTransformer((schema, context, ct) =>
{
    if (schema.Properties is not null)
    {
        foreach (var property in schema.Properties)
        {
            if (schema.Required?.Contains(property.Key) != true)
            {
                // Nullable property removed; instead clear
                // the Null flag from the type enum
                property.Value.Type &= ~JsonSchemaType.Null;
            }
        }
    }
    return Task.CompletedTask;
});
```

### Summary of changes

| .NET 9 (OpenAPI.NET v1) | .NET 10 (OpenAPI.NET v2) |
|---|---|
| `new OpenApiString("1.0")` | `JsonValue.Create("1.0")` |
| `using Microsoft.OpenApi.Any` | `using System.Text.Json.Nodes` |
| `schema.Nullable = true/false` | `schema.Type \|= JsonSchemaType.Null` / `&= ~JsonSchemaType.Null` |
| `new OpenApiSecurityScheme { Reference = new OpenApiReference { Type = ReferenceType.SecurityScheme, Id = "oauth2" } }` | `new OpenApiSecuritySchemeReference("oauth2")` |
| `new() { [scheme] = scopes }` (dict syntax) | `new() { Scheme = ..., Scopes = ... }` |

If you need to stay on OpenAPI 3.0 output, you can also set `options.OpenApiVersion = OpenApiSpecVersion.OpenApi3_0;`, but the **code-level API changes above are still required** regardless of the spec version.
